{"year":"2026","content":[{"type":"text","content_text":"The 79th edition was held on February 22, 2026, at the Royal Festival Hall in London, hosted by Alan Cumming for the first time. <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 1054867, 'screen_type': movie}\">One Battle After Another</a> (2025) led the nominations, with 14, and won six awards, including Best Film, as well as Best Director and Best Adapted Screenplay for <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 4762, 'screen_type': person}\">Paul Thomas Anderson</a>. <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 1648346, 'screen_type': person}\">Robert Aramayo</a> won Best Leading Actor for <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 1317149, 'screen_type': movie}\">I Swear</a> (2025) and also took the EE Rising Star Award, and the Brazilian film <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 1220564, 'screen_type': movie}\">The Secret Agent</a> (2025) was nominated for Best Original Screenplay and Best Film Not in the English Language."},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Best Picture","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":1054867,"name":"Uma Batalha Após a Outra","image_path":"/2peYXW6CoruehDnKJGMjl2NuaNB.jpg","director":"Paul Thomas Anderson","winner":true,"backdrop_path":"/zpEWFNqoN8Qg1SzMMHmaGyOBTdW.jpg"},{"type":"movie","id":858024,"name":"Hamnet","image_path":"/njatIGrIlZCxB88UUBC2xgmfCNE.jpg","director":"Chloé Zhao","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":1317288,"name":"Marty Supreme","image_path":"/oLWBW1Sg9V8KGgbR3Y8jeEWF2Gi.jpg","director":"Josh Safdie","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":1124566,"name":"Sentimental Value","image_path":"/pTMpLRfB9wUaQ8CEdGEUkyVXwOo.jpg","director":"Joachim Trier","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":1233413,"name":"Sinners","image_path":"/v0Ljeti537c6cNKweuEN0iaU3x4.jpg","director":"Ryan Coogler","winner":false}]},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Outstanding British Film","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":858024,"name":"Hamnet: A Vida Antes de Hamlet","image_path":"/njatIGrIlZCxB8